<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hirohito</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Emperor Hirohito</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hirohito was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1926 until his death in 1989. His reign saw Japanese militarism, expansion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>. He announced Japan's surrender in 1945, and under the post-war constitution he remained emperor as a symbolic head of state, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> as a sovereign imperial system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hirohito.jpg" alt="Hirohito" width="286" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hirohito_in_dress_uniform_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
